ed","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-10-30","finding":"Critical Injury - Give First Aid or CPR: It was determined that a caregiver did not provide first aid to a child in their class when they became injured on the playground. The caregiver did not notify management of an injury and 30 minutes passed before the child received first aid.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026678166","violation_type_title":"Critical Injury - Give First Aid or CPR (26 TAC §746.3607(2))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1358821-i20260925-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1358821-i20260925","date":"2026-09-25","original_code":"746.1205(a)(5)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-10-30","finding":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Intervene to ensure each child's safety: It was determined that a caregiver did not intervene to ensure a child's safety. The caregiver did not respond to the needs of the child after they fell and injured themselves on the playground. The caregiver did not report the injury to management and just took the child back to class where they sat for thirty minutes before another staff intervened.","topic":"safety","source_record_id":"1026673042","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Intervene to ensure each child's safety (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(5))","topic_label":"Safety hazards"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1358821-i20260617","date":"2026-06-17","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":1,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905842632","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905842632","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2026-06-17","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1358821-i20260617-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-